# Context filter for the one image built from the REPO ROOT:
# bench/Dockerfile, which needs bench/ and pyhoglake/ together (bench
# installs the client from the sibling tree). server/ and webui/ build
# from their own directories and carry their own .dockerignore files.
#
# The first block is the one that has actually bitten: a host .venv is
# macOS-built binaries, and a copy of it into a linux image either
# fails at import or, worse, shadows the image's own install. Keep it
# out of the context entirely rather than relying on the Dockerfile not
# to COPY it.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.flox/

.git/
.github/

# Trees the bench image does not install. Excluded by name so the
# context stays small and a change over there cannot invalidate a
# layer here; add a line if a new top-level tree appears.
server/
webui/
duckdb-client/
hedgerow/
docs/

# Local run artifacts.
**/bench-results.jsonl
**/*.log
